# I use cron to enforce my time block boundaries and breaks as most of my work
# is being done on a PC and phone (I use an app to do sth. similar on my
# phone).
#
# Scheduled breaks help me to follow my priorities for the day/week (it
# sometimes takes me up to 15 min to "unfocus" resp. mentally park a task I was
# doing before I am able to do a focused prioritization). Leaving timing of
# breaks to cron helps me to concentrate as my brain is then not constantly
# reminding me of what else I need to do, and I can then trust my system that I
# will make right decisions during my planning & breaks.
#
# Advantages as opposed to only using alarms:
#   1. I don't have to think about my schedule and manage the alarms.
#   2. Alarms may go unnoticed (e.g. if my phone is in a different room or out
#   of battery).
#   3. There is no postpone button. I don't waste my willpower to keep my
#   time-blocks sharp.
#   4. I can always leave my PC on when I go away (it will turn off itself).
#   5. Easier context switches between time blocks in my day and clean desktop.
#
# Disadvantages of managing my daily schedule this way:
#   1. It is annoying during ONLINE CALLS - but this is also a blessing in
#   disguise as I am forced to stick online calls to my time-blocks, not the
#   other way around. However online calls need to be taken into consideration
#   when modifying this daily schedule.
#
#   Note: shutdown command uses a default "+1m" delay, hence if I am caught off
#   guard, I can return by turning my PC on back again and 1m is just enough
#   time to finish what I was doing.


*      0-6    * * *  root /sbin/shutdown

# --- 7 - 9 Time block 0 (phone on for 10 min) ---

50-59   8      * * *  root /sbin/shutdown

# --- 9 - 12 Time block 1 (phone off) ---

# --- Sext, lunch and walk (phone on) ---
*      12     * * *  root /sbin/shutdown

# --- 13 - 15 Time block 2 (phone off) ---

15,17  15     * * *  root /usr/bin/loginctl lock-sessions

# --- 15:30 - 17:40 Time block 3 (phone off) ---

# 17:40 - alarm on phone - supper

# --- 18:00 - 20:00 Bonus time block (optional, phone on)

*      20-23  * * *  root /sbin/shutdown


# === WEEKLY SCHEDULE ===
# Saturday
*      18-20  * * Sat  root /sbin/shutdown
# Sunday - rest/sport
*      12-20  * * Sun  root /sbin/shutdown

